<BaseLayout title="Vegas Loop" description="Official coverage of Vegas Loop developments.">
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a href="/sections">← All sections</a></p>
  <span class="card-category" style="margin-top: 1rem; display:inline-block;">Vegas Loop</span>
  <h1 class="section-title" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Vegas Loop</h1>
  <div class="article-body" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
    <p>Vegas Loop is The Boring Company’s underground transit system in Las Vegas, Nevada. It currently operates stations serving the Las Vegas Convention Center and nearby resorts, with further expansion underway.</p>
    <p>Under this section Tunnelati covers only primary sources: official posts from @boringcompany, relevant Elon posts that clearly address Vegas Loop, official boringcompany.com updates, and named public documents such as county or city votes and permits.</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 1.2rem;">What you will find here</h2>
    <ul style="margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
      <li>New station entitlements and approvals</li>
      <li>Tunnel construction progress and machine updates tied to Vegas</li>
      <li>Airport and key destination connections</li>
      <li>Operational and safety announcements from official sources</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not invent plans, ridership numbers, or timelines. Every claim is attributed to an official source.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>